<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. above consolidated financial results of Group have been reviewed and recommended by Audit Committee and approved by Board in their respective meetings held 27.01.2021.  nconsolidated financial results are prepared in accordance with Ind AS, as applicable and guidelines issued by SEBI. Ind AS are prescribed u/s133 of Act read with Rule 3 of Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules, 2015, and Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) (Amendment) Rules, 2016. said financial results represent results of PSP Projects Limited (“the Company”), its subsidiaries (together referred to as “the Group” and its share in results of JV which have been prepared in accordance with Ind-AS 110 – “Consolidated Financial Statement” and Ind AS 28 – “Investment in Associates and Joint Ventures”).  naforesaid unaudited consolidated financial results have been subjected to limited review by joint statutory auditors of Holding Company.  n2. During quarter, Group’s operations recovered further from economic slowdown caused by COVID-19 pandemic.Group has made assessment of recoverability of the Company’s assets such as Trade receivables, unbilled revenue, and Inventories, using reasonably available information, estimates and judgements and has concluded that there are no material adjustments required in interim financial results. However, impact assessment of COVID-19 is continuous process, given uncertainties associated with its duration and nature. impact thereof might be different from that estimated as at the date of approval of these financial results. Group will continue to closely monitor changes to future economic conditions.  n3. Group is primarily engaged in one business segment viz. construction/project activities, as determined by chief decision maker in accordance with Ind AS 108, Operating Segments. operations of  Company is predominately domiciled in India and therefore there are no reportable geographical segment.  n4. Indian Parliament has approved the Code on Social Security, 2020 which would impact the contributions by Group towards Provident Fund and Gratuity.Ministry of Labour and Employment has released draft rules for Code on Social Security, 2020 on 13.11.2020 and has invited suggestions from stakeholders which are under active consideration by Ministry. Group will assess the impact and its evaluation once subject rules are notified and will give appropriate impact in its financials in period in which, said code becomes effective including related rules framed thereunder to determine financial impact are published.  n5. Previous period figures have been regrouped/rearranged, to correspond to current period’s presentation.  n6.standalone financias forperiod ended 31.12.2020 are available on Company’s website (www.pspprojects.com)  nKey Standalone financials information is given below:                                                         Rs. in Lakhs  nParticularst                                       Quarter ended t          Half year ended t    nt                                       31.12.2020    31.12.2019   31.12.2020   31.12.2019    n                                                       (Unaudited)   (Unaudited)   (Unaudited)   (Unaudited  n  nTotal Incomet                       39,395.76      42,883.72     75,324.15 1,06,067.65 t  nProfit Before Tax and   nExceptional Itemt                       4,127.38         4,881.32      5,684.23    12,827.98 t     nProfit Before Tax and  n after Exceptional Itemt        3,853.27        4,881.32      5,410.12    12,827.98 t     nNet Profitt                                         2,791.83 t 3,674.77     4,010.45    9,499.44 t      nOther Comprehensive Income/(Loss)  (3.26)t (0.52)t     (9.77)      (1.56)              nTotal Comprehensive Incomet       2,788.57         t     3,674.25   4,000.68    9,497.88</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
